<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Diocese of Dresden-Meissen</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Diocese of Dresden-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meissen">Meissen</a> is the Catholic diocese of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, with its seat at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dresden">Dresden</a>. It continues the bishopric of Meissen, founded in 968, whose Catholic remnant survived the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Reformation</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-lusatia">Upper Lusatia</a> under the dean of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bautzen">Bautzen</a>. The diocese was re-established in 1921 and took its present name in 1980.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/diocese-of-dresden-meissen.jpg" alt="Diocese of Dresden-Meissen" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Brunswyk · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dresden_Hofkirche_abends_(2005).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
